    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c5c926413d71b3527bef17ac3136ab9f7b502fd2451fc1193c9c86cf26b4bf6b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A cited finite RH verification supplies the height boundary T0, after which a candidate zero is expressed in normalized variables and handled by the analytic kernel inequality; negativity of the accumulated correction and monotonicity of K reduce the higher-zero regime to an endpoint computation whose improved reciprocal bound is reused as R. The later autocorrelation kernel passes the same reported checks and, after four iterations, gives the source's best stated constant R0=5.68371.",
