    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c8a1c4f161404cede7e0d32d529e2e7f9ca869a4d41b922b9d121cb80b1db53f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source presents a staged reduction in which a nonnegative trigonometric weighting turns the prime side into an explicit-formula inequality, Stechkin pairing and transform positivity make one class of non-target zeros discardable, zero density and four correction terms budget the remaining contributions, a cited low-zero verification restricts the analytic case to heights above T0, and scaling the test function converts the assembled inequality into a monotone scalar-kernel bound that is fed back to improve R.",
